# bare_unit_name.z -- a FILE unit is reached by a qualified path, never by a
# bare name. `core` is a unit of this program's closure, so the binding names
# something real, but nothing in scope here claims that name: `u` binds with
# no type (its entry row says `notype`). The program root the
# file units hang under carries no unit-frame bit and no name edge, which is
# what keeps it out of the bare-name walks -- this pins that.
main: function is {
    u: core
    v: 1
    print "\{v}"
}
